--- body ---
## Context

Umbrella 0096 (align spec, PEP, and manual) closed 2026-05-08 with 7
child tickets. Since then, several PRs landed that changed validator
behavior, error formats, and struct layout (0116 schema-literal, 0117
merge parse/validate, 0118 tighten types, 0124 line numbers). These
may have introduced new divergences between:

- tickets/spec-erg-v1.md (normative format spec)
- pep-erg-v1.md (rationale document)
- docs/erg-manual.md (generated by erg --help --all)
- Go implementation (source of truth)

## Action

Re-run the alignment audit: diff spec claims against actual validator
behavior for each rule (1-13). Flag any divergence.

## Decision needed

Author must decide which document wins when spec and code disagree —
the 0096 convention was "align spec with behavior" but that may not
hold for every case.

## Audit Findings

### Rule-by-rule alignment table (spec vs code)

Rules are numbered per `erg validate` / `erg-manual.md`.

| Rule | Description | Spec | Code | Manual | Verdict |
|------|-------------|------|------|--------|---------|
| 1 | Magic first line `%erg 0.1` | Defined | `magicLine` const | Documented | ALIGNED |
| 2 | Required headers: Title, Created, Author (non-empty) | Defined | `parseErgBytes` checks | Documented | ALIGNED |
| 3 | No unknown headers | Closed set in header table | `v1HeaderKeys` map; `Tags:` and `Status:` get specific migration advice | Documented | ALIGNED |
| 4 | Non-repeatable headers appear at most once | Spec table marks Title/Created/Author/Closed as `no` | `v1SingletonKeys` matches | Documented | ALIGNED |
| 5 | Tag values from vocabulary | Spec hardcodes `needs-human, deferred` | Code uses `effectiveTagSet(cfg)` which defers to .ergrc `[tags]` section, falling back to `defaultTags` | Manual documents .ergrc override | **DRIFTED** (A) |
| 6 | Closed: non-empty, preamble only | Defined | `parseErgBytes` enforces | Documented | ALIGNED |
| 7 | Created is ISO date YYYY-MM-DD | Defined | `isoDateRE` | Documented | ALIGNED |
| 8 | Filename matches NNNN-slug.erg | Defined | `filenameRE` | Documented | ALIGNED |
| 9 | Blocked-by grammar (local-ref / forge-ref) | ABNF grammar in spec | `parseRef` + `hostRE`/`identRE` | Documented | ALIGNED |
| 10 | Local Blocked-by refs resolve to existing IDs | Defined | `validateCorpus` checks | Documented | ALIGNED |
| 11 | Log line format | Defined | `logLineRE` | Documented | ALIGNED |
| 12 | Both separators required; first occurrence is separator | Defined (incl. rule-12 relaxation) | `parseErgBytes` section walk | Documented | ALIGNED |
| 13 | No dependency cycles | Defined | `detectCycles` | Documented | ALIGNED |

12 of 13 rules are ALIGNED. Rule 5 has a documentation gap (drift A below).

### Cross-document drift table

| ID | Location | Issue | Severity |
|----|----------|-------|----------|
| A | Spec header table, row for Tag | Hardcodes values `needs-human, deferred`. Code defers to `.ergrc` via `effectiveTagSet`; manual documents `.ergrc [tags]` override. Spec does not mention configurability. | Medium |
| B | PEP section 12 heading | Heading reads "Tags header" (plural). Code and spec use `Tag:` (singular). Section 2 is already aligned (uses "Tag" singular). | Low |
| C | PEP section 12 body | Says `A Tags: header was added`, `Tags is repeatable`, and argues `Renaming to Tag: (singular) would weaken this` — actively opposing the rename that already shipped. | Medium |
| C2 | PEP section 12 body | Lists 4 enum values (`needs-human, deferred, post-talk, post-conference`). Code defaults only accept `needs-human, deferred`; `post-talk` and `post-conference` are rejected without .ergrc override. | Low |
| D | PEP metadata | `Modified: 2026-04-04` is stale (last spec edit was 2026-05-12). | Low |
| E | ergspecv1.go:34 | Comment says `each Tags entry` — should be `each Tag entry`. | Low |
| F | erg.go:22, erg_test.go:250, ergspecv1.go:41, ref.go:79 | Four source comments reference `rules/tickets.md` which no longer exists (content is now in `tickets/spec-erg-v1.md`). | Low |

### Child tickets to create

1. **Spec rule 5: document .ergrc tag override** — Drift A. Spec header table should note that the vocabulary is configurable via `.ergrc [tags]`.
2. **PEP section 12: fix Tags-to-Tag rename drift** — Drifts B, C, C2. Heading, prose, and enum values need updating.
3. **PEP: update Modified date** — Drift D.
4. **Fix stale source comments (Tags entry + rules/tickets.md refs)** — Drifts E and F. Grouped to avoid ticket spam.
